35,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"@All, the data is clear. Outreach averaged forty visitors, exceeding midweek main building figures. Winter closures did not disrupt community hall timetables.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"@All, the bus links are gone! Residents face an hour’s round trip. Yet remote catalogue use peaks after nine, when we lock up. We’re missing them!","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,George,,"@All, the grant pays only twelve months, then the flat budget absorbs the cost. The vehicle line overran by a third. The structure is the trap.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,"@All, the digitisation project failed, but the evening groups thrive. Yet we lock up at nine while remote use peaks later. We’re ignoring the actual demand.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"@All, the retired technician is gone, and no one on payroll can supervise. We cannot add tasks without checking who actually holds the skills.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Yumi, the bus gap is severe, but my data shows community halls survived winter closures. We must build where access already exists, not where we hope it will.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Ryuji, I agree! But we can’t just build where we are. We must reach them where they are. The remote peak proves they want us, just not at our hours.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,George,,"@Yumi, the remote peak is a symptom of our rigid hours. But the vehicle overrun proves we cannot fund new routes. We must stay within the flat budget’s limits.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"@George, the flat budget is a cage, but the evening groups prove people will show up if we meet them. We just need to stop locking the doors at nine.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@May, I hear you. But if no one can supervise the new facilitators, extending hours just adds risk. We must ensure the skills are present first.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Daisuke, supervision is critical, but my data shows community halls maintained timetables despite closures. We must leverage existing, resilient infrastructure rather than creating new, fragile dependencies.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Daisuke, I understand the risk! But the remote peak shows they are already self-managing. We just need to unlock the doors, not add new staff.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,George,,"@Daisuke, supervision is a cost, not a barrier. My data shows the vehicle line overran, but the equipment allocation closed under budget. We have reserves to fund training, not new routes.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, the evening groups already run unaided. That’s the proof. We don’t need new supervisors; we need to trust the model that already works.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"@May, I appreciate the trust. But the retired technician’s absence is a gap, not a style. We must verify who holds the certification before extending anything.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"@All, I will finalize my assessment. The data confirms that existing community infrastructure is resilient. We must anchor any expansion in those proven, self-sustaining locations to avoid seasonal fragility.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Yumi,,"@All, I’ll finalize my assessment. The data proves demand exists beyond our walls and hours. We must expand access to meet people where they actually are, not where we assume they are.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,George,,"@All, I will finalize my assessment. The grant’s twelve-month cliff and the vehicle overrun prove the structure is broken. We must choose an expansion that fits the flat budget, not one that breaks it.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,May,,"@All, I’ll finalize my assessment. The six-year-old programmes prove that self-sustaining models survive, while top-down projects rot. We must choose the expansion that already works, not the one that sounds impressive.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"@All, I will finalize my assessment. The data shows a critical gap in supervision and certification. We must choose an expansion that relies on existing, verified skills, not new, untrained commitments.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
